course: dictionary
lesson: 7823
title: Context clues: quinine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around a new word, because they are its context and often give clues. «Quinine, from the bark of the cinchona tree, was known to Andean peoples and became the main medicine for malaria for centuries.» The words bark, tree and medicine tell you that quinine is a medicine made from tree bark.
explain: Test your guess by swapping it into the sentence. Put "a medicine made from tree bark" in place of quinine and read it again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. If it does not, look for more clues or check a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Quinine» is a bitter medicine made from the bark of the cinchona tree.
fact: «Quinine» was used for a long time to treat malaria.
fact: Quinine gives tonic water its bitter taste.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Quinine, from the bark of the cinchona tree, was known to Andean peoples.» What is quinine? | A type of bread eaten in the Andes | A kind of cloth | *A bitter medicine made from tree bark | A sweet fruit from the mountains
exercise: «...became the main medicine for malaria for centuries.» What was quinine used for? | To make cloth blue | *To treat malaria | To sweeten drinks | To grow maize
exercise: «Quinine gives tonic water its bitter taste.» What does quinine give tonic water? | Its name | Its sweet taste | Its colour, always pink | *Its bitter taste
test: Find one word in «Quinine, from the bark of the cinchona tree» that tells you where quinine comes from. | malaria | centuries | main | *bark
test: «Andean peoples knew that cinchona bark helped with fever, which gave the world quinine against malaria.» What did Andean peoples know? | *Cinchona bark helped with fever | Quinine grows on potatoes | Malaria was a kind of tonic water | Maize was a kind of medicine
exam: Quinine is a bitter ___ made from the bark of a tree. Which word fits best? | colour | sweet | game | *medicine
